<p>The Omega name was an attempt to find a middle ground between the actual use of the greek alphabet poetically, with Omega representing &quot;the end&quot;, being at the end of the article, and the end of the series of univeres leading to the end, and the actual use of Omega in ordinal arithmetic were it is the first infinite cardinal/ordinal.</p>
